---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RailIndex from '../components/RailIndex.astro';

const reviewed = '19 September 2026';

// Os títulos têm de bater LITERALMENTE com os <h2> do corpo — checagem 22.
const sections = [
  { id: 'collect', title: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'do-not-collect', title: 'What we do not collect' },
  { id: 'browser-storage', title: 'What is stored in your browser' },
  { id: 'rights', title: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'would-change', title: 'What would change this page' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — mazetick"
  description="What mazetick collects, stated item by item: no cookies, no advertising, cookieless analytics, self-hosted fonts."
>
  <header class="mast">
    <p class="mono kicker">Notice</p>
    <h1 class="display title">Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="spread">
    <div class="body">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This page describes what this site does <strong>today</strong>. It is written
          from the site's own source rather than from a template, and it names the
          conditions that would make it out of date at the bottom.
        </p>

        <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>

        <h3>Analytics</h3>
        <p>
          We use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>. It does not use cookies, does
          not fingerprint your browser or device, and does not create a persistent
          identifier for you. It cannot follow you to any other site. It reports pages
          viewed and referring sites in aggregate. Serving it requires a small script
          from <code>static.cloudflareinsights.com</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use it for one reason, stated plainly: we set ourselves written targets for
          whether this site is worth continuing, and those targets are expressed in
          monthly visits. A target you cannot check is decoration.
        </p>

        <h3>Server logs</h3>
        <p>
          The site is served from Cloudflare's network as static files. Like any web
          server, Cloudflare processes your IP address and request in order to deliver
          the page. We do not receive that data as a per-visitor record and we do not
          combine it with anything else.
        </p>

        <h3>Fonts</h3>
        <p>
          Typefaces are served from this site's own domain. There is no request to Google
          Fonts or any other font host, so viewing a page here does not disclose your IP
          address to a third party for typography.
        </p>

        <h2 id="do-not-collect">What we do not collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>No cookies</strong> — neither our own nor anyone else's. See <a href="/cookies">Cookies</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>No accounts.</strong> There is nothing to sign up for and no password to store.</li>
          <li><strong>No advertising</strong> and no advertising network.</li>
          <li><strong>No affiliate links</strong> and no click tracking.</li>
          <li><strong>No forms.</strong> Contact is by email, which reaches us directly and is not processed by this site.</li>
          <li><strong>No selling or sharing</strong> of anything about you, because there is nothing held to sell or share.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="browser-storage">What is stored in your browser</h2>
        <p>
          At most one key, <code>mazetick:theme</code>, holding the word{" "}
          <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code>. It remembers that you chose a colour
          theme by hand. It is stored by your browser in local storage, it never leaves
          your device, and it never reaches our server. If you have not used the theme
          control, nothing is stored and the site follows your system setting. Clearing
          your browser's site data removes it, and the site works normally without it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under UK and EU data protection law you have rights of access, correction and
          erasure over personal data held about you. We hold none, so there is nothing
          for us to return or delete. If you email us, we hold that email; ask and we
          will delete it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="would-change">What would change this page</h2>
        <p>
          Any of the following, and this page must be revised <em>before</em> the change
          goes live rather than after:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Introducing advertising of any kind, including Google AdSense.</li>
          <li>Adding affiliate or referral links, or any tracking of clicks out.</li>
          <li>Adding a contact form, a newsletter or an email alert.</li>
          <li>Replacing or supplementing the analytics described above.</li>
          <li>Embedding anything served from another domain, including video or social widgets.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Several of those are on the roadmap. This notice exists so that the page cannot
          quietly stop being true when they arrive.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this page: <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="rail">
      <div class="rail-block">
        <span class="rail-label">As of</span>
        <p class="rail-note"><span class="stamp">Last reviewed {reviewed}</span></p>
      </div>
      <RailIndex items={sections} />
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
